<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anne of Brittany</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1477">1477</a>–<a href="/years/1514">1514</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anne of Brittany was duchess of Brittany from 1488 and twice queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, through marriage to Charles VIII in 1491 and Louis XII in 1499. She worked to preserve the duchy's separate status. Her daughter Claude married the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/francis-i">Francis I</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edict-of-union">Edict of Union of 1532</a> joined Brittany to the Kingdom of France.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anne-of-brittany.jpg" alt="Anne of Brittany" width="320" height="410" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean Bourdichon · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BNF_-_Latin_9474_-_Jean_Bourdichon_-_Grandes_Heures_d%27Anne_de_Bretagne_-_f._3r_-_Anne_de_Bretagne_entre_trois_saintes_(d%C3%A9tail).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
